[h1]Cities and Borders[/h1]
National borders, capitals, cities and naval bases of the mission's date on the tactical map – the Soviet Union, East and West Germany, Yugoslavia, Leningrad and Bonn, Holy Loch and Cam Ranh Bay. The stock map shows coastlines only.

[b]This mod only draws on the map. It changes nothing in the game or in any mission – and what it draws is a reference map, not the rules of your mission. Please read "Read this first" below.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Land borders as they were on the mission's date[/b]: the Soviet Union whole (the Baltic states apart from September 1991, the other republics from December 1991), the inner-German border and West Berlin until October 1990, Yugoslavia until 1991–92, Czechoslovakia until 1993, North and South Yemen until May 1990, the Vietnam DMZ until 1976; Eritrea, South Sudan, East Timor, Hong Kong and Macau by their years. Disputed borders and lines of control (Korea, Kashmir, the Golan, Cyprus) are dashed.
[*][b]Cities and bases[/b]: capitals of the time (East Berlin and Bonn before October 1990; the Soviet republics' capitals, Kiev and Riga among them, are not national capitals until the Union ends), cities, naval bases with an anchor in the colour of their side – blue for NATO and its allies, red for the Warsaw Pact – and air bases. Names follow the date: Leningrad, Gorky, Karl-Marx-Stadt, Bombay, Peking before 1979. Bases only in the years they were used (Holy Loch until 1992, Cam Ranh Bay Soviet 1979–2002, Kings Bay from 1979).
[*][b]Optional coastal distance line[/b] (off by default): a dashed line 3, 6 or 12 nm off the coast as the game's map draws it, around islands too.
[*]The same line width at every zoom, names that never overlap, a light colour set for the night map. Unit symbols, waypoints and the map's own labels stay on top.
[/list]

[h2]Read this first – what the lines are and are not[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]The mod changes nothing in the game or in any mission.[/b] No rules of engagement, no triggers, no zones, no scoring – nothing about what your units see or do. It only draws.
[*][b]Missions set their own areas and rules, and they often differ from real geography.[/b] [i]Northern Vigil[/i], for example, announces "weapons free" when two Soviet vessels enter its own 10 nm circle around a point – not when they cross the coast or a border. [i]Don't Mess With Texas[/i] fails the mission for attacking an airbase. [i]Operation Trident[/i] has an exclusion zone off Karachi. In missions that say "don't escalate" or "hold fire", [b]follow the briefing and the mission's own map areas (the game's Map Layers → On Map Areas), never a line from this mod.[/b] A ship crossing a border or the distance line drawn here is not a violation in the game unless the mission says so – and the other way round.
[*][b]Borders[/b] are present-day lines with date rules: approximate and simplified, drawn as Natural Earth draws disputed ones. Land borders only – [b]no sea borders, no airspace, no zones[/b]. The Berlin Wall and the Vietnam DMZ are hand-drawn and only approximate.
[*][b]The coastal distance line is not a territorial limit.[/b] It is one distance from the game's own coastline, the same for every country. In 1985 Norway claimed 4 nm, the United States and the United Kingdom 3, Greece and Turkey 6 in the Aegean, the Soviet Union 12, Libya the whole Gulf of Sidra – and states measure from baselines across bays and fjords, not from the shore. Use it as a ruler, not as a border.
[*][b]Cities, capitals and bases[/b] come from the game's own lists plus public data. A base on the map doesn't mean the mission models it, and the labels are public Cold War locations – [b]not intelligence about the mission's forces[/b]. Units and contacts are exactly as the game shows them.
[/list]

[h2]Where the data comes from[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Land borders[/b]: [url=https://www.naturalearthdata.com/]Natural Earth[/url] 1:10m boundary lines, public domain (release 5.1.2). The date rules (which borders existed when) are the author's own.
[*][b]Inner-German border, North/South Yemen, West Berlin[/b]: from Natural Earth's state lines (the old Länder, today's governorates). [b]Berlin Wall and Vietnam DMZ[/b]: drawn by hand, approximate.
[*][b]Cities, ports and airfields[/b]: the game's own campaign lists, read from your install when a mission starts – nothing of the game's data is copied or shipped.
[*][b]More cities and capitals[/b]: Natural Earth populated places, public domain. They carry today's populations, so the ranking of the cities of 1985 is not exact.
[*][b]Naval bases with side and years[/b]: the author's own list, approximate positions.
[*][b]Coastal distance line[/b]: computed in the game from the game's own world grid; nothing of the game's terrain is shipped.
[/list]
Made with Natural Earth. Free vector and raster map data at naturalearthdata.com.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
Open the map in a mission. Switch the layers in the map menu (≡) → Map Layers → [b]Borders[/b] and [b]Cities and bases[/b], or with [b]Shift+F7[/b] (borders) and [b]F7[/b] (cities). The coastal distance line is off until you set [i]Coastal distance line (nm)[/i] to 3, 6 or 12 in the config.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[b]Anchor Chain[/b] is required: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3380210757]subscribe[/url] and follow its [url=https://seapower-modders.github.io/AnchorChain/install-anchor-chain.html]installation guide[/url] (one manual step: copy its preloader into the game folder).

[h2]Settings[/h2]
[i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowerborders.cfg[/i] – for borders: toggle key, era (the mission's date or today's borders), disputed lines, line width, opacity, coastal distance line; for cities: toggle key, density, naval bases, air bases, civil airports, label size.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Sea Power 0.8.7. Tested with Topographic Map, Better TacMap, Rats Radio and Rats Pop-Out Windows loaded.

[b]The 3D-globe map of the 11 November update:[/b] the package also holds a second DLL for the new map (the public beta of 26 October 2026). It has been run in the game on that beta, but Anchor Chain 1.1.0 does not start there yet, so for players the mod can only load on the beta once Anchor Chain is updated. Each DLL stays off on the game version it is not for; the log says which one runs. Leave both in the folder.

No game files are changed; if a game update breaks one of the mod's hooks, the mod says so in the log and stays out of the way.

[h2]Problems?[/h2]
Please post the file [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] with your report, and tell me the mission and the date it starts on.

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerBorders]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerBorders[/url]
